{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Chem170Column",
    "description": "The WRF-Chem chem_opt = 170 (CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP) chemistry column, gas and aerosol together: the CBM-Z gas column (couplings/cbmz_column.esm: CBM-Z lifted over the 59 layers with emissions, Wesely dry deposition and large-scale wet scavenging), MOSAIC's gas-particle partitioning over the column's 59 levels x 8 sections (couplings/mosaic_column.esm: phase state, liquid thermodynamics, MESA salt rates, ASTEM's rates) and MOSAIC's aerosol chemistry (couplings/mosaic_aerchemistry_column.esm: nucleation, coagulation, aerosol dry deposition), joined through the units WRF moves a gas between them in.\n\nWHAT IS MOUNTED. The three columns' state-holding models by ref (CBMZColumn; GasParticle = mosaic_column.esm's Column; AerChem = mosaic_aerchemistry_column.esm's Column), every component they mount, wired by the same coupling libraries those documents import (lib/cbmz_column_processes.esm, lib/mosaic_gas_particle_processes.esm, lib/mosaic_aerchemistry_processes.esm, plus CBM-Z's peroxy pool and the emissions_driver libraries) and the same operator_compose that lifts CBM-Z onto the column; Host (mosaic_host_mapping.esm, mapaer_tofrom_host) for the gases' units; and Join.\n\nTHE JOIN. Down: the sixteen gases mapaer_tofrom_host maps leave CBMZColumn's molec/cm^3 states as WRF's chem values, ppmv = X/conv (the KPP interface's conv); Host forms their mole fractions rsub = chem/factgas and cairclm = rho_phy/factdens; ASTEM reads H2SO4, HNO3, HCl and NH3 in nmol/m^3, rsub * conv1a with map_mosaic_species' conv1a = cairclm * 1e6 * 1e9 (CBM-Z has no MSA, so ASTEM's fifth gas is zero), and nucleation reads H2SO4 and NH3 as rsub. Up: ASTEM's gas tendencies (GasParticle's Rates.dgas, nmol/m^3/s) over conv1a, plus nucleation's H2SO4 and NH3 uptake (AerChem's dh2so4_dt, dnh3_dt, mole fraction per second), times factgas * conv: the aerosol_<X> terms CBMZColumn adds to the column tendencies of H2SO4, HNO3, HCl and NH3, so its observeds d<X>_dt are the whole column's. The aerosol: Join.dr_dt is AerChem's component tendency plus ASTEM's condensation into the matching component (H2SO4 -> SO4, HNO3 -> NO3, HCl -> Cl, NH3 -> NH4) over conv1a.\n\nONE STATE. WRF applies emissions, dry deposition, KPP, MOSAIC (ASTEM, then nucleation, then coagulation) and wet scavenging in sequence within a step, each from the state the previous one left; the tests compare the instantaneous column tendency against every process's tendency at ONE state, each replayed there (tools/fill_chem170_column_tests.py; data/eqwefic/chem170_full/replay_joint.py). That state is the one ASTEM forms its fluxes at, so ASTEM's own in-model rates are references on every level whose eight fluxes were formed at it.\n\nSTILL INPUTS (what the Fortran's solvers decided, as in couplings/mosaic_column.esm): the Kelvin water activity ah2o_a and MESA's solid on path 6 (implicit equations, EarthSciIntegrator's job; couplings/mosaic_{kelvin,mesa}_equilibrium.esm state them), and ASTEM's dp_wet. The aerosol state is handed to the two MOSAIC parts twice, as GasParticle's ASTEM-box quantities (totals after conform_electrolytes, nmol/m^3) and as AerChem's rsub mixing ratios: conform_electrolytes and the rsub -> aer box mapping (map_mosaic_species, imap = 0, for the aerosol) are not transcribed, so the document does not derive one from the other; the tests hand it both, from the same state.\n\nWHAT IS NOT HERE. Vertical mixing (vertmx, needs EarthSciDiscretizations PR #53), photolysis computed by Madronich (the j-values are inputs), section moving (branch mosaic/movesect, EarthSciDiscretizations PR #54), aerosol emissions and aerosol wet scavenging (the emissions_driver's MOSAIC half is mounted, as in cbmz_column, but its aerosol tendency is not added to Join.dr_dt; wetdep_ls runs on sulf only), the water and phase changes MOSAIC makes by re-equilibrating (not rates), and N2O5's heterogeneous uptake (off in chem_opt = 170's defaults).",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "chem_opt-170",
      "cbm-z",
      "mosaic",
      "column",
      "coupling"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte."
    },
    "NSLOT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 65,
      "description": "Gas slots of chem_opt 170, numgas = 65 (slot 1 the dummy)."
    },
    "NBIN": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 8,
      "description": "MOSAIC size sections per cell (nbin_a; 8 in chem_opt = 170)."
    },
    "NEL": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 22,
      "description": "MOSAIC electrolytes."
    },
    "NZSR": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 19,
      "description": "Electrolytes that hold water, the first nsalt + 4."
    },
    "NSALT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 15,
      "description": "Soluble salts."
    },
    "NAER": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 112,
      "description": "MOSAIC aerosol species per bin (chem_opt = 170)."
    },
    "NCOMP": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 10,
      "description": "Components per section."
    },
    "NQ": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 12,
      "description": "Composition columns carried through coagulation: NCOMP components, the hysteresis water and the water."
    }
  },
